{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And this is My remembrance for generation to generation.</b> It refers back to <b>the Elohim of Abraham, the Elohim of Isaac, and the Elohim of Jacob</b>, for He will never forget the covenant of the fathers, and for all the generations, whenever they invoke \"the Elohim of Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob,\" El will hear and answer them (Psalms 55:20). And by way of truth, <b>this is My name forever</b> — the Elohim of Abraham, the Elohim of Isaac; <b>and this is My remembrance</b> — and the Elohim of Jacob; and therefore the vav is added upon it. And this is the reason that <b>זִכְרִי לְדֹר דֹר</b> (My remembrance for generation to generation) is deficient [in its letter count], and the enlightened will understand."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:01:57.074796139Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}